From: Alexey Belkov <alexey.belkov@jetbrains.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 14:47:40 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] [SLC] Generate @JvmOverloads for actual with inherited
 defaults

`createMethodsJvmOverloadsAware` and the synthetic no-arg constructor logic
decide whether a value parameter is optional via
`KaValueParameterSymbol.hasDeclaredDefaultValue`. That property is `false` for
an `actual` declaration whose default values are declared on the `expect`
(they cannot be repeated on the `actual`), so no @JvmOverloads variants and no
synthetic no-arg constructor were produced for such declarations, diverging
from the compiler's bytecode.

A plain switch to `hasDefaultValue` would be wrong: that property is also
`true` for parameters whose default is inherited from an *overridden*
function, but @JvmOverloads has no effect on an override (the overloads belong
to the base declaration, the compiler even reports
OVERLOADS_WITHOUT_DEFAULT_ARGUMENTS). Besides, `hasDefaultValue` does not
propagate `expect` defaults for *constructor* parameters.

Introduce `defaultParameterValueMask`:
a parameter counts as having a default if it is declared on the parameter
itself, or - for an `actual` declaration - on the matched `expect` parameter.
Overrides are intentionally excluded. The helper is used by both the
function/constructor overload generation and the synthetic no-arg constructor
helpers.

^KT-57537 Fixed

